# Previous and next navigation

Previous and next links connect ordered pages and include the destination context. [Official publishing guidance](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/components/previous-and-next-navigation/).

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation; they do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## When to use it

Use this navigation for chapters in installation or recovery guidance. Use native date controls for Energy periods and native pagination controls for a results table; they are not automatically the same pattern.

## Structure and behaviour

Give the navigation landmark a distinct name. Include both direction and destination title in each link. On the first or last chapter, omit the unavailable direction instead of adding an inert link. Decorative arrow artwork is optional; words must carry the meaning.

## Home Assistant boundary

Moving between guide pages must not submit a form or issue a device command. The examples use real section anchors to demonstrate ordering inside one isolated page. A production multi-page guide needs durable URLs and a consistent chapter list.

